.el .ds Aq '
.TH ifg-commit 1  "ifg-commit 0.9.1"
.SH NAME
ifg\-commit \- Write commits on the server without a local checkout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg commit\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write commits on the server without a local checkout
.PP
Every commit command names the branch and the commit it must still be at (`\-\-expected\-sha`, the full 40\-character SHA you read). If the branch moved, the server refuses with 409 REF_ADVANCED and writes nothing; it never creates the branch. `\-\-dry\-run` runs every check and prints what would happen without writing. Commits made through a token that belongs to an agent are authored as that agent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ifg\-commit\-create(1)
Commit many file changes as one commit
.TP
ifg\-commit\-apply\-patch(1)
Apply a unified diff as one commit
.TP
ifg\-commit\-cherry\-pick(1)
Apply the change an existing commit made, as a new commit
.TP
ifg\-commit\-revert(1)
Apply the inverse of an existing commit\*(Aqs change, as a new commit
.TP
ifg\-commit\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.9.1
